---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import NavBar from "../components/NavBar.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why not just prompts? | ContentFlow App"
  description="Why an operator app is more reliable than prompting alone."
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <NavBar />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why not only prompts?</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Prompts help ask questions. Workflow keeps momentum.</h1>
        <p>
          Better prompts can improve one interaction. They do not replace the need
          for resilient states, queued action paths, and review gates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <article class="price-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">What prompts do well</p>
          <h2>Increase immediate output quality</h2>
          <p>
            They help generate better first drafts, clearer ideas, and sharper
            suggestions per interaction.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="price-card accent-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">What prompts do not solve</p>
          <h2>Operational continuity under load</h2>
          <p>
            They do not preserve workspace context, queue states, or explicit
            recovery paths when upstream services temporarily fail.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <article class="doc-card">
          <h3>Human-in-the-loop is non-negotiable</h3>
          <p>
            ContentFlow App keeps publish-ready preparation explicit: review,
            status transitions, scheduling, and final validation remain operator-driven.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-card">
          <h3>Resilience is part of the product</h3>
          <p>
            Degraded mode is built into the workflow because backend availability
            is not guaranteed, and continuity is how teams actually win over time.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Short Version</p>
        <h2>Prompts are a tool. Workflow is the operating model.</h2>
        <p>
          ContentFlow App adds the operator surface your team needs after prompts:
          clear state, recovery, and reliable action execution.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/about">Read why it exists</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/skills">See workflows</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/faq">Open the FAQ</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
